;
; ===========================================================================
; Metal Armors sheet — head (WORN_HEAD), torso (WORN_ARMOR), hands
; (WORN_HANDS), feet (WORN_FEET2). All four slots are already independent in
; doWear (capacity 1 each, no cross-slot conflict logic), so a full
; helm+cuirass+gauntlets+boots set can already be worn simultaneously with no
; engine change. PARAMETER1 is the DR% (same convention as existing armor,
; e.g. illithium armor INUMBER 306 PARAMETER1 75); PARAMETER2 is the
; Weaponsmithing skill level doCraft actually reads for ARMOR (see the header
; note above). Accessory pieces (gauntlets/boots) are set noticeably lower
; than the torso piece at the same DR% tier — less material, less
; construction — even though the stat itself is identical.
;
; Great Helm — full head coverage, heaviest.
