; ===========================================================================
; Misc. Items sheet. Robe and Bracers already exist as real Type ARMOR items
; in the original 1990s data (multiple robe archetypes across ITEM1/ITEM2/
; ITEMARM.SCR on WORN_BODY; bracers on WORN_WRIST in CHASSO.SCR/ITEM2.SCR) —
; nothing to add there. Shoulder Guards also already exists: INUMBER 560 in
; ITEM3.SCR (NAME 322 "guards", WORN_BACK, PARAMETER1 10), which force-sets
; ITEMADJ3=551 ("shoulder") on WEAR via script so it always displays as
; "shoulder guards" — that's the old-engine equivalent of what ADJECTIVE now
; does declaratively. There's a second ITEM3.SCR "guards" archetype, INUMBER
; 561 (WORN_DON, PARAMETER1 3, no adjective-forcing script, and dropped as a
; monster skin via SKINITEM 980 5 561 0 0 in MONSTERS.SCR) that looks like an
; unfinished/abandoned thigh guards, but per the user it's being left alone
; in case it has an undiscovered original purpose. So Thigh Guards below is a
; brand-new archetype, NOT a fix to 561 — item 560's structural twin for legs
; rather than shoulders, sharing its "guards" noun (322) and flat 10% DR (no
; leather/metal material tiers, matching how 560 itself has none), but
; CRAFTABLE since unlike 560 it's meant to enter the new crafting framework.
;
; Thigh Guards — legs, companion piece to the existing Shoulder Guards (560).
